{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1231138-continual-light-how-to","id":1231138,"title":"Continual Light: How to?'","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-29T10:04:16-07:00","id":1231138,"title":"Continual Light: How to?'","content":"In D&amp;D, one of the most popular spells around is <i>continual l</i><i>ight</i>, or in later editions <i>continual flame.</i> I've been thinking about how to do this in Mage, using something less than Forces 5. My current best attempt is a co-location portal to basically anywhere in space this side of Earth's orbit, using a Key to pass only light and possibly heat. Any other suggestions? Indefinite duration is a given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T10:11:39-07:00","id":1231140,"title":"","content":"I think you could pull it off using Forces 4, according to the chart room temperature and a flashlight are equivalent, so you should be able to just turn the ambient heat in an area into light. Again, indefinite duration is a given. Lower than Forces 4 I'm not sure other than Forces 2 Control Light which would allow you to take a dim light source and make it much brighter. Depending on the situation that might be feasible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23958-tengugrib","name":"TenguGrib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T10:43:55-07:00","id":1231149,"title":"","content":"Stick one Aether in a lightbulb?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T11:07:12-07:00","id":1231157,"title":"","content":"While the practical impact is minor, <i>free energy</i> is a pretty big deal.<br /> <br /> I do wonder if an unveiling of either Matter and/or Forces would let everyone know where objects are (and what &quot;color&quot; they are) in the vicinity would fit. It wouldn't really be <i>light</i>, but would basically work just like it for most purposes. It would need the Scale Spell Factor increased to cover the area-to-be-&quot;illuminated&quot;, but it could work. Run it as a combined Matter+Forces spell, and you can use the Matter 2 Attainment Permanence for easier Advanced Duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T11:08:41-07:00","id":1231159,"title":"","content":"Forces 3 could Weave kinetic energy to emit light, put the spell on a stick and wave it around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T11:20:22-07:00","id":1231164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1231138-continual-light-how-to?p=1231159#post1231159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forces 3 could Weave kinetic energy to emit light, put the spell on a stick and wave it around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Transform heat energy into light and you never have to worry about the refrigerator light staying on. Win-win.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T16:00:08-07:00","id":1231243,"title":"","content":"I wonder, could you use Veil of Moments on a glow stick or flashlight to make sure they continue to function but the power sources aren't used up ?<br /> <br /> I can think of only one way to do it with less than Forces 3. First you need a pair of rings made out of phosphorus. Now you pick a point in space and use a sensory Compelling of Matter to concentrate a good amount of oxygen into it, while also creating a small tunnel of concentrated air leading back to a point close to you. When you click the rings, a spark flies off them and into the tunnel, being carried by the highly combustible nature of concentrated air into the big pocket, where it explodes and generates light. So long as you keep feeding it a steady supply of air, it will keep exploding and producing light. On a small scale and with a long duration, you will have a continuous light source and be able to light things remotely. On a big scale, you will be playing as Roy Mustang from Fullmetal Alchemist. And, if you invest in both Arcana, then you can end up making perfected fire, which is very powerful indeed. Although, I recommend against making the spell lasting, because it will use a point of mana every time and you could end up asphyxiating everyone nearby, including yourself, by using up all the air.<br /> <br /> Can it be done without the rings ? Yes, you probably should, especially since you would need to put them away after every use or risk setting yourself on fire. A lighter can do the job, but it has limited fuel supply. Plus the rings just sound plain cooler <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-29-2018, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T21:32:24-07:00","id":1231296,"title":"","content":"What does the spell do, for people who don't play much D&amp;D? Judging by the name, making a fire/light not burn out itself would be a Perfecting spell So casting it on a torch would make the torch burn as long as the spell lasts unless doused, With patterning you could propably ignore the &quot;unless doused&quot; part and have a fire that burns forever, even with lack of oxygen/fuel/etc.<br /> <br /> A Shielding spell might make a fire more difficult to douse too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T08:53:05-07:00","id":1231378,"title":"","content":"The reason this doesn't come up much in Mage is that if you have Forces you may as well just give people Nightvision instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T10:27:59-07:00","id":1231388,"title":"","content":"It seems to me that a lot of the technique to make this light source depends on how you expect to use it. I like the idea of picking a spot in a room where the ambient heat (70\u00b0?) simply draws into a conversion of light continuously. If it's a big-enough room you won't really have to worry about the room growing 'too' chilly, since heat will seep in from the greater world around and reach an equilibrium, end effect being a 'cool' room. That added effect could be useful too, for other purposes. That being said, what you get is a stationary light. You could make it mobile I suppose.<br /> <br /> The phosphorous tool sounds wonderfully geeky, though some Academics skill may be needed.<br /> <br /> It all comes down to this, in my mind. The lower your dots in Forces, the more cleverness you'll employ to find your work-arounds in lieu of simply making light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>..............","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21103-mindflower","name":"Mindflower","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T10:02:31-07:00","id":1231604,"title":"","content":"Control Light would be enough. Cast it on a crystal, and you can cause ambient IR to enter the crystal, at which point the spell shifts it up the spectrum to visible. There's always at least enough IR around (if only from the person needing the light) to produce the equivalent output of a 100W incandescent bulb. At the very worst, two spells will do the job: one to gather and one to shift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T11:16:30-07:00","id":1231611,"title":"","content":"I suppose it is too complicated to just buy a flashlight for everyone and thus not risk paradox?<br /> <br /> Sorry for the sarcasm. Anyway, you could find a Forces ley line and have it perpetually power up your lights. And many other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T11:33:59-07:00","id":1231617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1231138-continual-light-how-to?p=1231611#post1231611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, you could find a Forces ley line and have it perpetually power up your lights. And many other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>You would need a Node, not just a singular ley line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T20:24:41-07:00","id":1231716,"title":"","content":"Couldn't Matter Perfecting be used for on alkaline or lead acid based batteries to cause them to &quot;reset&quot; into their new unused state, and if transformation was cyclically to occur each Ritual Interval that could lead to continual output until disrupted? Also note with the default Scale being assumed size 5, that's either a large pile of batteries or a very large one. Side benefit is dispelling the magic just prevents the renewal cycle and doesn't cause it to immediately lose power, as the batteries likely will have mundane charge based of their type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T05:30:39-07:00","id":1231772,"title":"","content":"This thread is slowly showing us that one thing more dangerous than a mage is a mage who knows how physics work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T05:38:23-07:00","id":1231774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1231138-continual-light-how-to?p=1231772#post1231772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread is slowly showing us that one thing more dangerous than a mage is a mage who knows how physics work.</div> </div> </div> </div>The lack of this actually being reflected in the setting leads me to believe that it's actually of minimal impact - probably because magic operates on symbolism, not physics - though they're not (always) mutually exclusive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T06:02:31-07:00","id":1231781,"title":"","content":"Spells themselves has no regards for physics, but knowing physics can allow you to use spells in even more creative way.<br /> <br /> Still, not sure if Matter can be used that way. I don't have the book on me right now, but I believe Matter has problems creating high energy matters. At least the four dot transformation spell explicitly can't transform into volatile matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T06:10:22-07:00","id":1231783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1231138-continual-light-how-to?p=1231774#post1231774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lack of this actually being reflected in the setting leads me to believe that it's actually of minimal impact - probably because magic operates on symbolism, not physics - though they're not (always) mutually exclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it does explain why mages see each other as so dangerous. Law of symbolism wins at the end of the day, but law of physics helps us get there. (Until we get to Disciple-hood. Then physics tend to sit in the corner.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T06:16:40-07:00","id":1231785,"title":"","content":"All in all, I'd say that certain Skills can supplement certain Arcana, but the Arcana can just as well compensate for lack of those Skills. No Computer dots? Just use Forces to force the computer to do what you want. Many Computer dots? Then you better know the extent of what you can do with computers when using Forces.<br /> Which is one reason why people with high Mind are scary. On top of Mind being on of the ruling Arcana for the Devil Path, and able to both mind control you (through both soft and hard mind control) and erase your memories of being manipulated, it can also grant the mage massive amounts of Skill dots. Beyond what's humanly possible if they spend a Reach on going beyond Power Stat imposed limits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T07:01:35-07:00","id":1231794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1231138-continual-light-how-to?p=1231785#post1231785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All in all, I'd say that certain Skills can supplement certain Arcana, but the Arcana can just as well compensate for lack of those Skills. No Computer dots? Just use Forces to force the computer to do what you want. Many Computer dots? Then you better know the extent of what you can do with computers when using Forces.<br /> Which is one reason why people with high Mind are scary. On top of Mind being on of the ruling Arcana for the Devil Path, and able to both mind control you (through both soft and hard mind control) and erase your memories of being manipulated, it can also grant the mage massive amounts of Skill dots. Beyond what's humanly possible if they spend a Reach on going beyond Power Stat imposed limits.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://imgflip.com/i/2d9p3n\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"https://imgflip.com/i/2d9p3n\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"https://imgflip.com/i/2d9p3n\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"https://i.imgflip.com/2d9p3n.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T08:24:02-07:00","id":1231817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1231138-continual-light-how-to?p=1231774#post1231774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lack of this actually being reflected in the setting leads me to believe that it's actually of minimal impact - probably because magic operates on symbolism, not physics - though they're not (always) mutually exclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's minimal impact in the setting for the same reason the real implications of science and technology have minimal impact in fiction: the authors and game designers aren't scientists. The original version of <i>Transmission</i> had &quot;radio waves&quot;, &quot;bluetooth&quot;, and &quot;wifi&quot; as different things (all three are EM waves that fall under the &quot;radio wave&quot; band of the spectrum); several currently existing things in the book are just wrong from a physics standpoint, and it's clearly not an intentional thing to push the supremacy of symbolism, it's just that someone with a high school level physics education grabbed some garbled something off Wikipedia.<br /> <br /> To be clear, this isn't a dig at anyone: <i>Mage</i> is a fantastically designed game and the people that worked on it are clearly good at what they do; but they're not scientists or engineers and it shows. And to read more into the inaccuracies than that they're inaccurate is silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T08:42:09-07:00","id":1231821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1231138-continual-light-how-to?p=1231817#post1231817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's minimal impact in the setting for the same reason the real implications of science and technology have minimal impact in fiction: the authors and game designers aren't scientists. The original version of <i>Transmission</i> had &quot;radio waves&quot;, &quot;bluetooth&quot;, and &quot;wifi&quot; as different things (all three are EM waves that fall under the &quot;radio wave&quot; band of the spectrum); several currently existing things in the book are just wrong from a physics standpoint, and it's clearly not an intentional thing to push the supremacy of symbolism, it's just that someone with a high school level physics education grabbed some garbled something off Wikipedia.<br /> <br /> To be clear, this isn't a dig at anyone: <i>Mage</i> is a fantastically designed game and the people that worked on it are clearly good at what they do; but they're not scientists or engineers and it shows. And to read more into the inaccuracies than that they're inaccurate is silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some things might be mistakes (such as mentioning different types of radio waves), but many others are intentional departures from physics because symbolism literally is how Supernal magic works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T08:08:10-07:00","id":1232125,"title":"","content":"Seeing as it's right in the setting that Supernal laws supersede Fallen laws I consider it forgivable when they make scientific mistakes. I don't expect everyone to understand all the nuances of physics, I myself make mistakes and forget things rather frequently despite my Bachelor of Physics. That said I haven't found any unforgivable mistakes that I can recall, and mostly just little inconsistencies that can be easily ignored or dismissed under the premise of the first sentence of this paragraph. <br /> <br /> I do agree though, the more you know about physics the more you can get really creative. I suspect someone with indepth knowledge of biology could do similar with Life magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23958-tengugrib","name":"TenguGrib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T09:36:42-07:00","id":1232156,"title":"","content":"I'm still not sold on the idea of advanced scientific knowledge meaningfully impacting how creative you can get, or rather, I suspect that as that level of knowledge grows higher, you're going to be subject to diminishing returns. Having a solid fundamental understanding of how the Fallen World works is probably an advantage, an advanced degree in Physics is likely less so.<br /> <br /> You might have the right understanding of Forces to know that it's reasonable to Compel a particle to behave in a certain way, and that if you did, it would cause a chain reaction that leads to a much more forceful effect, but at the end of the day, odds are good that that won't actually work, because the <i>symbolic</i> change you're enacting is aligned more with Patterning, for example, than Compelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T10:41:36-07:00","id":1232170,"title":"","content":"Nah. Spells doesn't care about indirect side effects. If Compelling is the right Practice for your effect, that's the Practice you're able to use. Patterning might be able to do the same thing, but without the painstaking efforts you underwent to set up the conditions that allows the Compelling spell to work.<br /> For example: In order to gain dangerous amounts of radiation you probably need Forces 4 (Transform Energy should work even though the chart lacks radiation), but if you've somehow procured a piece of uranium close to but below critical mass and know your physics, then you'd be able to cast a Shielding spell on the uranium to prevent free neutrons from escaping it, thereby decreasing the threshold for critical mass and setting off a nuclear explosion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T11:16:49-07:00","id":1232181,"title":"","content":"Except that Shielding spells are specifically for protection, which can lead to some debate on what exactly is being protected, I'd agree with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T11:26:46-07:00","id":1232184,"title":"","content":"Edited: I summarized this better below.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 07-03-2018, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T11:33:21-07:00","id":1232189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1231138-continual-light-how-to?p=1232170#post1232170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Compelling is the right Practice for your effect, that's the Practice you're able to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>To better summarize my above post: I agree with this.<br /> <br /> I disagree that Shielding is the right practice for your effect in your example, because I the effect, as I read it, is to set off a nuclear explosion. Everything else is 'how' the magic achieves it, which the guidance in the book tells us to disregard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First and foremost, decide exactly what you\u2019re trying to accomplish with your spell. Don\u2019t focus on how the magic will do what you want for now, just focus on what you want it to do. </div> </div> </div>Advanced scientific knowledge does a great job of explaining a lot of different 'how's, but that's of minimal usefulness to my reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 07-03-2018, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T12:03:42-07:00","id":1232198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1231138-continual-light-how-to?p=1232189#post1232189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To better summarize my above post: I agree with this.<br /> <br /> I disagree that Shielding is the right practice for your effect in your example, because I the effect, as I read it, is to set off a nuclear explosion. Everything else is 'how' the magic achieves it, which the guidance in the book tells us to disregard.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Advanced scientific knowledge does a great job of explaining a lot of different 'how's, but that's of minimal usefulness to my reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want my spell to Shield the Protons and Neutrons in the atoms that make up this hunk of iron from the strong interaction.<br /> <br /> I know that the side effect of this is a giant explosion, but the explosion itself is not part of the Imago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T12:14:53-07:00","id":1232203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1231138-continual-light-how-to?p=1232198#post1232198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I want my spell to Shield the Protons and Neutrons in the atoms that make up this hunk of iron from the strong interaction.<br /> <br /> I know that the side effect of this is a giant explosion, but the explosion itself is not part of the Imago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I mean...I can't see that as being anything other than disingenuous.<br /> Everyone at the table knows what you're actually trying to do.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, the people I play with are like-minded, we all find that this reading makes sense, and it's held up pretty well over the several hundred hours of Mage 2E we have going so far. If allowing technicalities like that works for you without looking too closely at the implications for the setting, more power to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 07-03-2018, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T12:22:50-07:00","id":1232204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1231138-continual-light-how-to?p=1232203#post1232203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I mean...I can't see that as being anything other than disingenuous.<br /> Everyone at the table knows what you're actually trying to do.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, the people I play with are like-minded, we all find that this reading makes sense, and it's held up pretty well over the several hundred hours of Mage 2E we have going so far. If allowing technicalities like that works for you without looking too closely at the implications for the setting, more power to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not any more &quot;disigenuous&quot; than using Forces 2 to throw a ball of fire in someone's face (something you can do), your Imago is &quot;control fire&quot; (two dots) and the result is &quot;deal lethal damage&quot; (a four dot effect).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T12:26:40-07:00","id":1232205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1231138-continual-light-how-to?p=1232204#post1232204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not any more &quot;disigenuous&quot; than using Forces 2 to throw a ball of fire in someone's face</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with both the validity of the comparison and the thought process behind it, but I don't think we need to derail the thread any further.<br /> You do what works for you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T18:39:43-07:00","id":1232522,"title":"","content":"One can think of it as a tradeoff. Technically speaking, any mage can meditate into a mind, convince the proper goetia to lock down certain memories until a keyphrase is uttered and fool whoever investigates that mind. Sure, someone with Mind can do it easier, but that will leave nimbus traces and could be more easily dispelled. So what is the tradeoff ? That you need to go into a mind, which may not be the safest place (generating Paradox if its a sleeper's), takes longer and is more difficult. So you get a better solution, but you need to earn it via roleplaying.<br /> <br /> Similarly, you can transmute seawater into fresh water, but it takes more raw power to do it permanently, whereas a bit of scientific knowledge can give the idea to separate the salt from the water. By the same token, you could use Shielding that way, but where are you going to get the uranium ? Where did your character get that knowledge ? Does someone/something guard it against mages who tried this kind of stuff before ? All that can be used to flesh out your character and create interesting stories. Likewise, a mage who studies a lot about karma and history could create some innovative Fate spells. Its an interesting space to explore so long as it can be properly justified in character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T18:53:50-07:00","id":1232525,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a>: I think that the question of &quot;does someone/something guard against mages who tried this kind of stuff before?&quot; is the most interesting. Even if you subscribe to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3570_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3570\" data-vbnamecard=\"3570\">lnodiv</a>'s viewpoint, it would still be relatively easy for any starting mage to cause massive destruction by sneaking in to a military installation and using magic to cause a launch of conventional weapons. That a few terrorist Mages haven't managed to cause humanity to completely destroy themselves and/or plunge the world into absolute chaos indicates that, at the very least, there are Masters on every side that actively work to maintain some semblance of the status quo.<br /> <br /> Also, nuking everything isn't a terribly useful solution to the overwhelming majority of problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 07-04-2018, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T19:06:14-07:00","id":1232529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1231138-continual-light-how-to?p=1232525#post1232525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a>: I think that the question of &quot;does someone/something guard against mages who tried this kind of stuff before?&quot; is the most interesting. Even if you subscribe to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3570_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3570\" data-vbnamecard=\"3570\">lnodiv</a>'s viewpoint it's would still be relatively easy for any starting mage to cause massive destruction by sneaking in to a military installation and using magic to cause a launch of conventional weapons. That a few terrorist Mages haven't managed to cause humanity to completely destroy themselves and/or plunge the world into absolute chaos indicates that, at the very least, there are Masters on every side that actively work to maintain some semblance of the status quo.<br /> <br /> Also, nuking everything isn't a terribly useful solution to the overwhelming majority of problems.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep, the way I like to think about it is, if any character does anything outrageous, there may draw negative attention from bigger fish, and this being CofD, there is always a bigger fish. If they are lucky, they stumble into a failsafe and are just spooked away, or they may end up hunted by Banishers, Seers, archmagi, an ochemata, be drawn into a contest with the True Fae, be targeted by the God Machine, a high rank Spirit, powerful vampires, etc.I like to imagine that stumbling into the terrifying things that lurk in the dark and seeing the price they paid for being unwise is how even the most hubristic mages get the importance of some caution beat into them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-04-2018, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T19:17:33-07:00","id":1232532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1231138-continual-light-how-to?p=1232525#post1232525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a>That a few terrorist Mages haven't managed to cause humanity to completely destroy themselves and/or plunge the world into absolute chaos indicates that, at the very least, there are Masters on every side that actively work to maintain some semblance of the status quo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think this is one of those joint threats (like Scelesti) that both the Pentacle and Seers would actively watch for and try to put a stop to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T10:12:10-07:00","id":1233456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1231138-continual-light-how-to?p=1232189#post1232189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To better summarize my above post: I agree with this.<br /> <br /> I disagree that Shielding is the right practice for your effect in your example, because I the effect, as I read it, is to set off a nuclear explosion. Everything else is 'how' the magic achieves it, which the guidance in the book tells us to disregard.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Advanced scientific knowledge does a great job of explaining a lot of different 'how's, but that's of minimal usefulness to my reading.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually yeah, thinking more on it I agree with you. A basic understanding (read Highschool or maybe 1st year college) is helpful. Anything higher than that offers diminishing returns and you're right that most of the added understanding would have to get discarded in light of the rules for how magic works (specifically the idea of symbolic truth bearing more weight than real world truth). Sure your ST might allow for some creative work arounds, but again, diminishing returns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23958-tengugrib","name":"TenguGrib","